WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:02.210
Hey, this is really weird.

00:00:02.210 --> 00:00:09.100
Speaking of cases, Donald Trump now says he
is honored, not horrified, not concerned.

00:00:09.100 --> 00:00:17.029
Trump is honored that we in the United States
have by far the most corona virus infections

00:00:17.029 --> 00:00:18.029
in the world.

00:00:18.029 --> 00:00:19.770
This is extremely odd.

00:00:19.770 --> 00:00:22.460
Here is the man himself saying it.

00:00:22.460 --> 00:00:25.289
So when we have a lot of cases, I don't look
at that as a bad thing.

00:00:25.289 --> 00:00:30.489
I look at that is in a certain respect as
being a good thing because it means our testing

00:00:30.489 --> 00:00:32.259
is much better.

00:00:32.259 --> 00:00:37.989
So if we were testing a million people instead
of 14 million people, we would have far fewer

00:00:37.989 --> 00:00:39.000
cases.

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:40.019
Right.

00:00:40.019 --> 00:00:42.980
So I view it as a badge of honor.

00:00:42.980 --> 00:00:44.450
This is absolutely crazy.

00:00:44.450 --> 00:00:45.450
Trump.

00:00:45.450 --> 00:00:47.520
Trump talks about this as an honor.

00:00:47.520 --> 00:00:52.719
He's not really honoring the victims or their
families when he continues to just flippantly

00:00:52.719 --> 00:00:56.519
remark about we've we've passed the peak.

00:00:56.519 --> 00:00:57.949
We figured it out.

00:00:57.949 --> 00:00:58.980
We're the best.

00:00:58.980 --> 00:01:01.160
We've got the most has the best test.

00:01:01.160 --> 00:01:02.380
We've got all the equipment.

00:01:02.380 --> 00:01:03.410
We've got all the different stuff.

00:01:03.410 --> 00:01:04.410
We're reopening.

00:01:04.410 --> 00:01:05.410
It's all great.

00:01:05.410 --> 00:01:06.410
We did so well.

00:01:06.410 --> 00:01:08.409
He doesn't seem to be honoring anyone.

00:01:08.409 --> 00:01:11.600
And Trump continues to be completely confused
about testing.

00:01:11.600 --> 00:01:13.409
He keeps talking about raw numbers.

00:01:13.409 --> 00:01:17.020
We've, you know, a million tests, 14 million
tests.

00:01:17.020 --> 00:01:20.189
Let's give this some serious thought, because
this matters.

00:01:20.189 --> 00:01:24.909
You know, Trump's wacky comment about a badge
of honor from having the most infections.

00:01:24.909 --> 00:01:28.260
It's not some is bonkers off the wall cuckoo
for Cocoa Puffs.

00:01:28.260 --> 00:01:31.579
But let's use it to actually get informed
about things.

00:01:31.579 --> 00:01:36.020
Let's not just dismiss it as the rantings
of a lunatic, which it is.

00:01:36.020 --> 00:01:42.090
But Trump's idea is we have so many infections
because we have so much testing.

00:01:42.090 --> 00:01:43.090
OK.

00:01:43.090 --> 00:01:44.090
Let's explore that.

00:01:44.090 --> 00:01:50.180
Let's look at the numbers of the five million
global confirmed coronavirus cases.

00:01:50.180 --> 00:01:52.020
The U.S. has about 1.6 million.

00:01:52.020 --> 00:01:58.369
So what we have in the U.S. is 32 percent
of the cases, but we only have 4 percent of

00:01:58.369 --> 00:01:59.369
the population.

00:01:59.369 --> 00:02:03.060
So the cases are out of sync with our population.

00:02:03.060 --> 00:02:05.359
Now we have more cases than the next.

00:02:05.359 --> 00:02:08.130
I think it's six countries combined globaly.

00:02:08.130 --> 00:02:10.039
The case numbers are crazy.

00:02:10.039 --> 00:02:16.019
But do we have the most cases because we have
the most testing?

00:02:16.019 --> 00:02:22.319
Well, not really in the sense that our testing
per capita is still only thirty eighth in

00:02:22.319 --> 00:02:23.319
the world.

00:02:23.319 --> 00:02:26.760
So what Donald Trump is claiming doesn't make
any sense.

00:02:26.760 --> 00:02:31.180
And we still are only testing about three
hundred and seventy five thousand people per

00:02:31.180 --> 00:02:32.180
day.

00:02:32.180 --> 00:02:33.370
I sound like a broken record.

00:02:33.370 --> 00:02:37.760
I've told you many times now we should have
been at 500 thousand a day more than a month

00:02:37.760 --> 00:02:38.760
ago.

00:02:38.760 --> 00:02:42.420
We need to get to five thousand five hundred
thousand a day to eventually get to one and

00:02:42.420 --> 00:02:45.240
a half to five million tests per day.

00:02:45.240 --> 00:02:49.150
That's what you need to really be doing, significant
surveillance testing where you would say,

00:02:49.150 --> 00:02:54.090
listen, regardless of symptoms, if you are
65 or older, you need to get it.

00:02:54.090 --> 00:02:55.500
Go and get a test this week.

00:02:55.500 --> 00:02:56.500
OK.

00:02:56.500 --> 00:02:59.540
Next week, if you are between 55 and 65, go
and get a test.

00:02:59.540 --> 00:03:03.510
You need one and a half to five million tests
today to be able to start doing that kind

00:03:03.510 --> 00:03:04.849
of surveillance testing.

00:03:04.849 --> 00:03:07.739
We are nowhere close to that even still.

00:03:07.739 --> 00:03:10.000
Let's move on to the next analysis.

00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:16.600
Maybe most importantly, there is no doubt
that case numbers do depend on testing, even

00:03:16.600 --> 00:03:20.440
if the U.S. is only 38 per capita in testing.

00:03:20.440 --> 00:03:22.500
But deaths do not depend on testing.

00:03:22.500 --> 00:03:30.069
And when you look at deaths per capita, the
United States is 12th highest in the world

00:03:30.069 --> 00:03:35.440
in deaths per capita out of more than one
hundred and eighty countries.

00:03:35.440 --> 00:03:40.280
As Donald Trump often likes to say, our deaths
per capita, not total deaths now.

00:03:40.280 --> 00:03:41.280
OK.

00:03:41.280 --> 00:03:44.140
Well, of course, we're number one in total
deaths, but that's that's different.

00:03:44.140 --> 00:03:46.909
We're talking about deaths per capita deaths
per capita.

00:03:46.909 --> 00:03:52.860
The United States is the 12th highest out
of more than 180 countries.

00:03:52.860 --> 00:03:56.140
So a lot of people have been writing to me
saying, David, you've got to talk about this

00:03:56.140 --> 00:03:57.140
with Joe Rogan.

00:03:57.140 --> 00:03:58.140
Next time you go on.

00:03:58.140 --> 00:04:02.220
I do hope that this comes up next time I go
on and talk with Joe Rogan about it.

00:04:02.220 --> 00:04:03.640
I want to get the data out there.

00:04:03.640 --> 00:04:09.650
And the frustrating thing about this is that
it's shocking how many people are making claims

00:04:09.650 --> 00:04:15.780
about cases, deaths, testing without understanding
that you can just go find the data very often.

00:04:15.780 --> 00:04:22.390
I will tweet a screenshot of testing numbers,
per capita deaths, you know, whatever.

00:04:22.390 --> 00:04:23.390
Right.

00:04:23.390 --> 00:04:24.390
